-- title:
--   Special-fibre components map onto closures of their generic points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^{2} \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is $1$, with $M/p \neq 0$; assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` (namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series with the integral $j$-coefficients) lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios of integral forms for $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the bundle of Deligne–Rapoport data for the two-chart integral model of $X_H(M)$ over $R p$ (properness, flatness, integrality and local finite presentation of the structure map, integral closedness of the sections on affine opens, a geometric curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the base change together with Galois equivariance and $q$-expansion normalisation of the charts, and smoothness and geometric integrality in the generic fibre; these and the remaining fields are summarised here). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R p \to A$ be a ring map compatible with the structure map $R p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a local commutative ring with a ring map $\rho_O : R p \to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ satisfy $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O = \mathrm{residue} \circ \rho$. For each $i \in \{0,1\}$, using the integrality of the curve $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho$, the conclusion is that the set-theoretic image of the composite of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho\,i$ with `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρO toκ htoκ` (the base-change comparison from the fibre over $\kappa_A$ to the model over $O$) equals the closure of the single point obtained by applying the further composite with $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho$ to the generic point of $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho).C$, and that this image is closed.
--
--   This is the statement that each of the two components of the geometric special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ at $p$ has closed image in the model over $O$, that image being the closure of the component's generic point $\xi_\infty$ or $\xi_0$. It is used in the local analysis of the crossing points of the special fibre, feeding the identification of maximal ideals as a branch ideal plus $(p)$ and the construction of oriented étale crossing charts.
